WEBVTT

00:00.630 --> 00:05.100
After you cross the troll's
bridge and you save the prince

00:05.100 --> 00:10.060
or princess, you return them
back to their father, the King.

00:10.060 --> 00:13.330
And he's so excited that you
returned their son or daughter

00:13.330 --> 00:17.430
to him that he wants to
throw a brunch in your honor.

00:17.430 --> 00:19.430
But he has a little
bit of a conundrum

00:19.430 --> 00:20.960
in throwing the brunch.

00:20.960 --> 00:27.731
He wants to figure out how
many cupcakes should he order?

00:27.731 --> 00:29.230
He doesn't want to
waste any, but he

00:29.230 --> 00:31.511
wants to make sure that
everyone has enough to eat.

00:31.511 --> 00:33.260
And you say, well
what's the problem here?

00:33.260 --> 00:35.509
And he says, well I know
adults eat a different number

00:35.509 --> 00:37.066
of cupcakes than children eat.

00:37.066 --> 00:39.190
And I know that in my
kingdom, an adult will always

00:39.190 --> 00:41.290
eat the same amount
and a child will always

00:41.290 --> 00:42.690
eat the same amount.

00:42.690 --> 00:45.255
And so you say, King, well what
information can you give me?

00:45.255 --> 00:47.130
I might be able to help
you out a little bit.

00:47.130 --> 00:50.110
You're feeling very confident
after this troll situation.

00:50.110 --> 00:57.680
And he says, well I know at the
last party we had 500 adults

00:57.680 --> 01:04.420
and we had 200
children, and combined

01:04.420 --> 01:10.220
they ate 2,900 cupcakes.

01:10.220 --> 01:11.944
And you say, OK,
that's interesting.

01:11.944 --> 01:14.110
But I think I'll need a
little bit more information.

01:14.110 --> 01:15.160
Have you thrown
parties before then?

01:15.160 --> 01:16.250
And the king says,
of course I have.

01:16.250 --> 01:17.257
I like to throw parties.

01:17.257 --> 01:19.090
Well what happened at
the party before that?

01:19.090 --> 01:24.840
And he says, well there
we also had 500 adults

01:24.840 --> 01:26.660
and we had 300 children.

01:29.002 --> 01:30.460
And you say, well
how many cupcakes

01:30.460 --> 01:31.501
were eaten at that party?

01:31.501 --> 01:37.200
And he says, well we know
it was 3,100 cupcakes.

01:37.200 --> 01:38.750
And so you get a
tingling feeling

01:38.750 --> 01:41.552
that a little bit of algebra
might apply over here.

01:41.552 --> 01:42.760
And you say, well let me see.

01:42.760 --> 01:44.010
What do we need to figure out?

01:44.010 --> 01:46.720
We need to figure out the
number of cupcakes on average

01:46.720 --> 01:48.260
that an adult will eat.

01:48.260 --> 01:56.750
So number of cupcakes
for an adult.

01:56.750 --> 02:00.220
And we also need to
figure out the number

02:00.220 --> 02:03.760
of cupcakes for a child.

02:03.760 --> 02:06.464
So these are the
two things that we

02:06.464 --> 02:07.880
need to figure out
because then we

02:07.880 --> 02:09.880
can know how many adults
and children are coming

02:09.880 --> 02:12.210
to the next branch that are
being held in your honor

02:12.210 --> 02:14.310
and get the exact right
number of cupcakes.

02:14.310 --> 02:16.310
So those are things you're
trying to figure out.

02:16.310 --> 02:18.360
And we don't know
what those things are.

02:18.360 --> 02:23.720
Let's define some variables
that represent those things.

02:23.720 --> 02:25.160
Well let's do a for adults.

02:25.160 --> 02:27.170
Let's let a equal the
number of cupcakes

02:27.170 --> 02:29.370
that, on average,
each adult eats.

02:29.370 --> 02:31.010
And let's do c for children.

02:31.010 --> 02:35.700
So c is the number of cupcakes
for a child on average.

02:35.700 --> 02:38.060
So given that
information, let's see

02:38.060 --> 02:41.810
how we can represent what the
King has told us algebraically.

02:41.810 --> 02:44.620
So let's think about this
orange information first.

02:44.620 --> 02:47.626
How could we represent
this algebraically?

02:47.626 --> 02:49.580
Well let's think about
how many cupcakes

02:49.580 --> 02:51.470
the adults ate at that party.

02:51.470 --> 02:54.670
You had 500 adults, and
on average, each of them

02:54.670 --> 02:56.520
exactly a cupcakes.

02:56.520 --> 02:58.730
So the total number of
cupcakes that the adults ate

02:58.730 --> 03:01.170
were 500 times a.

03:01.170 --> 03:02.420
How many did the children eat?

03:02.420 --> 03:03.460
Well same logic.

03:03.460 --> 03:08.360
You had 200 children and
they each ate c cupcakes.

03:08.360 --> 03:11.180
So 200 times c is the
total number of cupcakes

03:11.180 --> 03:12.320
that the children ate.

03:12.320 --> 03:13.500
Well how much did
they eat in total?

03:13.500 --> 03:15.249
Well it's the total
number that the adults

03:15.249 --> 03:17.370
ate plus the total number
that the children ate

03:17.370 --> 03:21.830
which is 2,900 cupcakes.

03:21.830 --> 03:24.830
So let's do that and apply that
same logic to the blue party

03:24.830 --> 03:26.760
right over here, this
blue information.

03:26.760 --> 03:30.690
How can we represent
this algebraically?

03:30.690 --> 03:33.410
Well once again, how many total
cupcakes did the adults eat?

03:33.410 --> 03:36.656
Well, you had 500
adults and they each

03:36.656 --> 03:40.115
ate a cupcakes, which
is an unknown right now.

03:40.115 --> 03:41.490
And then what
about the children?

03:41.490 --> 03:45.639
Well you had 300 children
and they each ate c cupcakes.

03:45.639 --> 03:47.180
And so if you add
up all the cupcakes

03:47.180 --> 03:50.670
that the adults ate plus all the
cupcakes that the children ate,

03:50.670 --> 03:53.984
you get to 3,100 cupcakes.

03:53.984 --> 03:55.650
So this is starting
to look interesting.

03:55.650 --> 03:56.910
I have two equations.

03:56.910 --> 04:00.360
I have a system of two
equations with two unknowns.

04:00.360 --> 04:02.570
And you know from your
experience with the troll

04:02.570 --> 04:04.440
that you should be
able to solve this.

04:04.440 --> 04:07.105
You could solve it graphically
like you did in the past,

04:07.105 --> 04:08.480
but now you feel
that there could

04:08.480 --> 04:10.480
be another tool in your
tool kit which is really

04:10.480 --> 04:13.850
just an application of the
algebra that you already know.

04:13.850 --> 04:17.440
So think a little bit about
how you might do this.

04:17.440 --> 04:19.800
So let's rewrite this first
equation right over here.

04:19.800 --> 04:30.110
So we have 500a plus 200c
is equal to 2,900 cupcakes.

04:30.110 --> 04:33.720
Now, it would be good if we
could get rid of this 500a

04:33.720 --> 04:34.530
somehow.

04:34.530 --> 04:38.090
Well you might say, well
let me just subtract 500a.

04:38.090 --> 04:41.770
So you might say, oh, I
just want to subtract 500a.

04:41.770 --> 04:44.040
But if you subtracted 500a
from the left hand side,

04:44.040 --> 04:46.519
you'd also have to subtract
500a from the right hand side.

04:46.519 --> 04:48.060
And so the a wouldn't
just disappear.

04:48.060 --> 04:49.950
It would just end up
on the right hand side,

04:49.950 --> 04:51.640
and you would still
have one equation

04:51.640 --> 04:54.190
with two unknowns which
isn't too helpful.

04:54.190 --> 04:55.720
But you see something
interesting.

04:55.720 --> 04:57.720
You're like, well
this is a 500a here.

04:57.720 --> 05:01.340
What if I subtracted
a 500a and this 300c?

05:01.340 --> 05:05.770
So if I subtracted
the 500a and the 300c

05:05.770 --> 05:06.880
from the left hand side.

05:06.880 --> 05:08.030
And you're like, well
why is that useful?

05:08.030 --> 05:09.890
You're going to do the same
thing on the right hand side

05:09.890 --> 05:12.550
and then you're going to have
an a and a c on the right hand.

05:12.550 --> 05:15.207
And you just say, hold on,
hold on one second here.

05:15.207 --> 05:17.040
Hold on, I guess you're
talking to yourself.

05:17.040 --> 05:18.640
Hold on one second.

05:18.640 --> 05:21.630
I'm subtracting the left
hand side of this equation,

05:21.630 --> 05:23.640
but this left hand side
is the exact same thing

05:23.640 --> 05:25.040
as this right hand side.

05:25.040 --> 05:28.050
So here I could
subtract 500a and 300c,

05:28.050 --> 05:33.140
and I could do 500a and
subtract 300c over here.

05:33.140 --> 05:35.570
But we know that
subtracting 500a and 300c,

05:35.570 --> 05:39.430
that's the exact same
thing as subtracting 3,100.

05:39.430 --> 05:40.690
Let me make it clear.

05:40.690 --> 05:47.060
This is 500a minus 300c
is the exact same thing

05:47.060 --> 05:52.260
as subtracting 500a plus 300c.

05:52.260 --> 05:56.920
And we know that 500a plus
300c is exactly 3,100.

05:56.920 --> 05:58.040
This is 3,100.

05:58.040 --> 06:00.640
This is what the second
information gave us.

06:00.640 --> 06:04.190
So instead of subtracting
500a and minus 300c,

06:04.190 --> 06:06.770
we can just subtract 3,100.

06:06.770 --> 06:07.720
So let me do that.

06:07.720 --> 06:09.260
This is exciting.

06:09.260 --> 06:11.390
So let me clear that out.

06:11.390 --> 06:12.860
So let's clear that out.

06:12.860 --> 06:15.270
And so here, instead
of doing this,

06:15.270 --> 06:19.380
I can subtract the exact same
value, which we know is 3,100,

06:19.380 --> 06:21.172
subtract 3,100.

06:21.172 --> 06:22.630
So looking at it
this way, it looks

06:22.630 --> 06:25.150
like we're subtracting
this bottom equation

06:25.150 --> 06:27.540
from the top equation, but
we're really just subtracting

06:27.540 --> 06:29.010
the same thing from both sides.

06:29.010 --> 06:31.180
This is just very
basic algebra here.

06:31.180 --> 06:34.920
But if we do that,
let's see what happens.

06:34.920 --> 06:38.940
So on the left hand side, 500a
minus 500a, those cancel out.

06:38.940 --> 06:44.280
200c minus 300c, that
gives us negative 100c.

06:44.280 --> 06:47.640
And on the right hand
side, 2,900 minus 3,100

06:47.640 --> 06:49.720
is negative 200.

06:49.720 --> 06:51.950
Well now we have one
equation with one unknown,

06:51.950 --> 06:53.500
and we know how to solve this.

06:53.500 --> 06:59.140
We can divide both
sides by negative 100.

06:59.140 --> 07:00.320
These cancel out.

07:00.320 --> 07:03.250
And then over here, you
end up with a positive 2.

07:03.250 --> 07:06.630
So c is equal to positive 2.

07:06.630 --> 07:08.510
So we've solved one
of the unknowns,

07:08.510 --> 07:12.010
the each child on
average drinks two cups.

07:12.010 --> 07:15.210
So c is equal to 2.

07:15.210 --> 07:17.274
So how can we figure
out what a is?

07:17.274 --> 07:18.815
Well now we can take
this information

07:18.815 --> 07:22.370
and go back into either one
of these and figure out what

07:22.370 --> 07:23.960
a has to be.

07:23.960 --> 07:26.560
So let's go back into the
orange one right over here

07:26.560 --> 07:29.550
and figure out what a has to be.

07:29.550 --> 07:38.710
So we had 500a plus 200c, but
we know what c is, c is 2.

07:38.710 --> 07:46.720
So 200 times 2 is
equal to 2,900.

07:46.720 --> 07:48.390
And now we just
have to solve for a,

07:48.390 --> 07:50.560
one equation with one unknown.

07:50.560 --> 07:55.540
So we have 500a,
200 times 2 is 400,

07:55.540 --> 07:59.100
plus 400 is equal to 2,900.

07:59.100 --> 08:02.570
We can subtract 400 from
both sides of this equation.

08:02.570 --> 08:03.880
Let me do that.

08:03.880 --> 08:10.620
Subtracting 400, and we are
left with this cancels out.

08:10.620 --> 08:13.200
And on the left hand
side, we have 500a.

08:13.200 --> 08:14.280
This is very exciting.

08:14.280 --> 08:15.540
We're in the home stretch.

08:15.540 --> 08:19.950
On the right hand
side, you have 2,500.

08:19.950 --> 08:22.330
500a equals 2,500.

08:22.330 --> 08:26.750
We can divide both
sides by 500, and we

08:26.750 --> 08:30.700
are left with 2,500
divided by 500 is just 5.

08:30.700 --> 08:33.690
So you have a is equal
to 5 and you're done.

08:33.690 --> 08:35.980
You have solved the
King's conundrum.

08:35.980 --> 08:39.390
Each child on average drinks
2 cups of water-- sorry,

08:39.390 --> 08:40.200
not cups of water.

08:40.200 --> 08:41.658
I don't know where
I got that from.

08:41.658 --> 08:46.140
Each child 2 cupcakes and each
adult will eat 5 cupcakes.

08:46.140 --> 08:47.439
a is equal to 5.

08:47.439 --> 08:49.730
And so based on how many
adults and children are coming

08:49.730 --> 08:52.670
to the brunch in
your honor, you now

08:52.670 --> 08:56.470
know exactly the
number of cupcakes

08:56.470 --> 08:59.970
that the King needs to order.
